## Task
Write a rule based on a clearly DIFFERENT idea from all rules above, likely to score higher.

response:
The rule uses a unified horizon-aware “deficit” score: each available robot is ranked by how far its projected duty count/hours would remain below the final per-robot target, so default rosters stay balanced without a special mixed-duty branch. On top of that it adds horizon-fit penalties for mixed duty lengths (avoiding dead remainders), a maintenance guard that defers a robot’s last duty before maintenance unless it can return or the fleet is capacity-tight, and a sorted new-robot list based on fit and maintenance/charge efficiency.

